WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.890
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.537
which takes about fifty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:10.725
You'll name the identity types the register
holds, and where each one is read from.

4
00:00:10.725 --> 00:00:14.627
You'll explain the program's
high, medium and low risk rule,

5
00:00:14.627 --> 00:00:17.450
and why a stale account
is only ever a lead.

6
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.075
You'll run the inventory against the
fixtures and read its high-risk findings.

7
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:24.786
And you'll show that the
reader refuses a call the

8
00:00:24.786 --> 00:00:27.362
task doesn't declare, and
a cloud it doesn't know.

9
00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:32.292
Before you start, read the guide's
track at a glance: for this track,

10
00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:36.663
the system inventory or C M D B
is the source of truth, not HR.

11
00:00:36.663 --> 00:00:40.500
And review Microsoft Automation
Module 1 on permissions.

12
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.600
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1 or later with
Pester 5, and a clone of the repository.

13
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.590
No tenant.
